{"episodes":{"189463":"A severe thunderstorm developed near Holyoke and produced hail up to 2 inches in diameter. Also, a brief tornado develop south of Akron.","189575":"Numerous strong to severe thunderstorms develop across southeast Wyoming on the afternoon of the 25th. One storm, which formed along a stationary boundary near the Wyoming/Nebraska border, ended up producing a brief, stationary tornado between Huntley and Lyman along with golf ball hail.","189720":"Severe thunderstorms brought damaging winds to much of Arkansas.","189960":"A strong thunderstorm produced hail up to penny size on the east side of Rapid City.","189962":"Thunderstorms developed over Fall River and Custer counties and quickly became severe as they formed into a line and crossed southwest South Dakota. The storms produced large hail and wind gusts to around 60 mph.","189963":"A thunderstorm briefly became severe over southeast Meade County, producing hail up to ping pong ball size east of Elm Springs.","189964":"A cluster of strong to severe thunderstorms developed across eastern Pennington County and tracked east-southeast into northwest Jackson County, producing wind gusts to around 60 mph.","190730":"In the early afternoon of the 25, multiple storms formed in eastern Colorado and northwestern Kansas and moved north-northeast. There were multiple clusters, or waves, of storms throughout the afternoon to overnight hours. These storms produced 1.75 Inch Diameter Hail, and Landspouts.","190817":"Thunderstorms produced large hail across portions of western Kansas on 04/25.","190840":"In the early afternoon of the 25th, multiple storms formed in northwestern Kansas and moved north-northeast. There were multiple clusters, or waves, of storms throughout the afternoon to overnight hours. These storms produced 3 inch diameter hail, 70 MPH thunderstorm wind gusts, and a tornado.","190943":"Several rounds of heavy rainfall lead to flash flooding of small creeks and streams. Rainfall amounts from 